# 3. Find Largest Even Number

### 🎯 Problem

Find the largest even number in an array.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class LargestEvenNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {5, 12, 8, 20, 15, 3};
        int largest = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
            if (arr[i] % 2 == 0 && arr[i] > largest) {
                largest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Largest Even = " + largest);
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Largest Even = 20
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
5  → odd ❌
12 → even → largest = 12
8  → even but 8 < 12 ❌
20 → even and 20 > 12 → largest = 20
15 → odd ❌
3  → odd ❌
```

### 🔑 Important Pattern

Combine a condition with maximum checking:

```java
if (arr[i] % 2 == 0 && arr[i] > largest)
```

### ⏱️ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# 4. Find Smallest Odd Number

### 🎯 Problem

Find the smallest odd number in an array.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class SmallestOddNum {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 15, 22, 7, 8, 13};
        int smallest = 0;
        boolean found = false;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] % 2 != 0) {

                if (!found) {
                    smallest = arr[i];
                    found = true;
                } else if (arr[i] < smallest) {
                    smallest = arr[i];
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Smallest Odd = " + smallest);
    }
}
```

### 🖥️ Output

```text
Smallest Odd = 7
```

### 🔍 Dry Run

```text
10 → even ❌
15 → odd → first odd → smallest = 15
22 → even ❌
7  → odd → 7 < 15 → smallest = 7
8  → even ❌
13 → odd → 13 < 7 ❌
```

### 🧠 Important Concept

We cannot simply use:

```java
int smallest = arr[0];
```

because `arr[0]` might not be odd.

Instead, we find the **first valid odd element**.

### 🔑 Pattern

```java
boolean found = false;
```

Then:

```java
if (!found) {
    smallest = arr[i];
    found = true;
}
```

After finding the first valid element:

```java
else if (arr[i] < smallest)
```

### ⏱️ Complexity

* Time: `O(n)`
* Space: `O(1)`

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

